# Shared style configuration, kept identical across datamatch, derivoce,
# taupatch, msomgom, dsfit, fancyfx and distsamp so a habit learned in one
# repository is the right habit in the next.
#
# Two defaults are deliberately changed.
#
# `line_length_linter(100)` is a gate, not the target. The target is 80, which
# this code mostly holds - about 1,500 lines run past it across the seven
# repositories, but only a hundred run past 100. Setting the gate at 80 would
# flag a wall nobody reads; setting it at 100 catches the lines that genuinely
# ran away while leaving the near-misses alone.
#
# `object_name_linter` is off because the naming split is deliberate rather than
# accidental. fancyfx exports plotEffects(), plotROC() and combinePlots(), and
# datamatch exports accessCopernicus() and matchData(); the rest of both
# packages is snake_case. Renaming public API for consistency would break every
# downstream call for a cosmetic gain, so the linter is told not to ask.
#
# `semicolon_linter(allow_compound = TRUE)` because pairing two short, related
# assignments on one line is used deliberately here and reads better than four
# lines would - `du_dx <- du[[2]]; du_dy <- du[[3]]` in derivoce,
# `lat1 <- rep_len(lat1, n); lon1 <- rep_len(lon1, n)` in distsamp. A *trailing*
# semicolon is still flagged, since that one is only ever a leftover.
linters: linters_with_defaults(
    line_length_linter(100),
    semicolon_linter(allow_compound = TRUE),
    object_name_linter = NULL
  )
exclusions: list("R/RcppExports.R")
